DESCRIPTION:Get your tickets now\n  \nWhat is it about Beethoven’s 9th Symp
 hony that sets it apart? Maybe it’s the innovative musical structure. Maybe
  it’s the way Beethoven blends themes of chaos\, redemption\, grace\, and s
 truggle so effortlessly. Or it could be that this piece culminates\, as Joh
 n Henken of the LA Philharmonic writes\, “expressing our highest aspiration
 s with music of life-affirming exaltation.” \nFor the first time in our his
 tory the BSO will perform Beethoven’s iconic 9th Symphony. Joined by a 100+
  member community chorus on the stage of Indiana University’s Musical Arts 
 Center (MAC)\, this is sure to be an unforgettable concert experience that 
 will also feature a world premiere piece by Daixuan Ai. \nParticipating cho
 irs include the Bloomington Chamber Singers (Caio Lopes\, director)\, Voces
  Novae (Sue Swaney\, director) and the choir of the Unitarian Universalist 
 Church (Sue Swaney\, director)\, as well as individuals from many other loc
 al choirs. The choirs are all coming together under the direction of Dr. Be
 tsy Burleigh. \nVocal soloists:Soprano: Nathalie FriederichAlto: Esther JoT
 enor: Suro KimBass: Stephen Stavnicky \nAdults: $25\, Students: $12\, Child
 ren under 18: Free\nSaturday May 16\, 2026\, at the IU Musical Arts Center\
 n6:15pm pre-concert talk\n7:00pm concert \nGet your tickets now
